  "finalReply": "Implemented `/app/attack.py:attack(encrypt_fn)` recovering `key[5]` via a deterministic 3-round differential.\n\n**Characteristic (prob 1, key-independent):** `F` maps `0x80800000→0x02000000`, `0x00008080→0x00000002`, `0x80808080→0x02000002` deterministically because `+0x80` equals `^0x80`. Chaining `B0=0x80808080, B1=0, B2=0x80808080` gives input diff `(A0,B0)=(0x02000002,0x80808080)` → after 3 rounds `(A3,B3)=(0x80808080,0x02000002)` with probability 1 (verified). Plaintext diff: `dL=0x02000002, dR=0x82808082`.\n\n**Last-round equation:** `B3=CL^CR`, `dF=dCL^0x80808080`, and `dF=F(B3^K5)^F(B3'^K5)` with known input diff `0x02000002`. True `K5` satisfies all pairs; wrong keys fail quickly.\n\n**Search:** 20 chosen-plaintext pairs, then brute-force only the 65536 `seed*1234567 & 0xFFFFFFFF` candidates with early abort. Tested 10/10 random keys, 0.01–0.11s, unique candidate, well under 30s.",
